tools/baremetal - what is downloaded for the bare-metal macOS 26 USB, fetched and checked, never vendored.

What:     the owner's PC (MSI B550-A PRO, Ryzen 7 5800X, RX 7800 XT, RTL8111 Ethernet, ALC897
          audio, Crucial P3 / P310 NVMe) boots macOS 26 Tahoe through OpenCore from a USB stick.
          fetch.sh downloads the pins below into ~/rdna3-baremetal/dl, build_efi.py builds the
          EFI folder from them, make_usb.sh writes the stick. docs/BAREMETAL.html is the procedure.
Format:   tools/baremetal/pins.txt (name, version, sha256, url) is what fetch.sh reads; this file is
          the reason for each pin. tests/test_baremetal.sh checks that they agree.
Pins:     all are official release builds, fetched and sha256 checked (BSD-3-Clause, except the
          Realtek driver, GPL-2.0, and Dortania's SSDT binaries, which are compiled from its MIT
          repository); a changed file is refused, not used.
