  macOS recovery: not pinned (Apple's servers, always the newest for the board): macrecovery.py
    -b Mac-27AD2F918AE68F61 (MacPro7,1) -os latest; the script verifies every chunk against
    BaseSystem.chunklist. Fetched 2026-10-29: macOS 26.6.2 (25G83), BaseSystem.dmg 960530321
    bytes, sha256 edddd0d5869caaa12e29e6996a04f11590280580976a119dbd42c24fa62fe18e.
Not used: WhateverGreen (no RDNA3 support, docs/INSTALL-OPENCORE.html section 6), USBToolBox /
    UTBMap (not needed: the 5800X board's two USB controllers have 14 and 8 root ports, both
    under macOS's limit of 15 per controller; docs/BAREMETAL.html), SMCProcessor, VoodooPS2.
AMD_Vanilla: the kernel patches come from tools/vm/data/amd_vanilla-a174cca.plist
    (tools/vm/data/amd_vanilla.SOURCE), the file the card VM runs.
Update:   take a newer release's zip sha256 from its GitHub release, set pins.txt and this file,
    run tests/test_baremetal.sh; check the plugin's kern_start.cpp still reaches the macOS in use
    and the Lilu minimum is met.
